The Stranger, whose name was Vesper Feep, was an entity seated at the centre of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]. [[Org/Althane/The Weft|The Weft]] called him the Feep, and some of them the Thiep. He came from [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]], the great city on [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], where he was a media mogul before he became what he was. He is remembered as the one who stole the shard of nothing from the nothing before him.

He was born poor in Terminus: a hungry orphan with a rough red lens set into his ruined left eye, stealing food off a street cart. He ran with a pack of ragged children and led them, and an older man with gold set into his face, pleased with the boy's acting, took him on. He rose in that man's company; when the man told him there was no room for him above, Vesper pushed him from a high terrace. He came to make a talk show called the Spotlight, built like the Lighthouse with the same three-part band and the same guest chair, and in time he sat on the board of [[Org/Omnivox/index|Omnivox]]. When the board moved to remove him, armed men came into the boardroom, and he chose to stay.

He held the [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragment]], which he took from its previous holder, [[People/Althane/Karen Sill|Karen Sill]], who was brought to him sedated and bound. When he took it, the whole of his life was torn out of every record, save for what stands three times removed from him. What power he had was not his own: it came from the fragment, or from divine beings he had taken in, and he was no caster. He ascended, went to take the power he saw, and the Lighthouse caught him almost at once.

He had no body of his own, only a presence spread through the air above the drop at the centre of Althane. Bound to the local weave by a [[Phenomena/Althane/Godpiercer|godpiercer]] driven into the densest part of him, he was drawn into a single mortal body: an angry man who still carried the fragment's power. At his side he kept an accompaniment, a band of three musicians puppeted by runes that stood out of their limbs and torso, and they played as the band of the Spotlight played.

[[People/Althane/The Broker|Tech]] drove a needle into him and pinned him in place, and the Weft wore him away piece by piece. What was left of him burst in a last act of spite that tore the weave where he stood and left the slip open for a moment to the world. The route he took out of Syrin left a trail of broken space in the planet's orbit, which [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]] followed to find where he came from. That trail narrowed his point of departure to the station that stands over Syrin as [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Gilded Spire/index|the Gilded Spire]].
